<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's Nov export prices fall 1.0 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's Nov export prices fall 1.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's export prices fell 1.0 percent in November from the previous month and were 5.2 percent lower than a year before, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The bureau said the index had fallen every month since January, except for a rise in August.</p>
<p>The November decrease was mainly due to the fall in wool and coal prices, partially offset by price increases for petroleum, the bureau said.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
